# UBS rapid bug gate: per-run artifacts written by scripts/ubs_gate.sh.
# Uploaded by .github/workflows/ubs.yml as run artifacts and read by nothing in
# the tree, so they are untracked. ubs-findings.txt WAS tracked, which meant every
# scan rewrote a 6,400-line committed file and left the tree dirty -- so a sibling
# running the gate produced a diff that looked like work and was only a timestamp.
ubs-findings.txt

# The generated views over that run. ubs-findings.json and ubs-new.md are
# rebuilt on every scan and are only ever consumed as run artifacts.
#
# ubs-history.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the accumulated fingerprint
# set that makes "new" mean "never seen before" rather than "absent from the last
# run", and accepting a finding is the act of committing the updated set. A gate
# whose history is gitignored would forget everything on every fresh clone.
ubs-findings.json
ubs-new.md

# BEAM build artifacts and the local container cache. _build and deps are
# resolved inside beam/ by the umbrella's mix.exs; .cache/ holds the bind mounts
# the BEAM CI job reuses between runs.
beam/_build/
beam/deps/
.cache/

# Editor/tool scratch written into the working tree. Not source, and not any agent's
# work product -- but leaving it untracked makes `make verify-clean` permanently red for
# everyone, and a gate that can never pass is a gate people learn to ignore. Same
# rationale as beam/_build and .cache above.
.zcode/
